    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "But I got in what people consider late because my daughter brain cancer came back that she had it four years old. And I took care of her and I only ran for politics to pay back my country by running for healthcare for everyone like we had in the military. When it came back this time, I wasn't going to get in originally. But I did after she got into a safe harbor in June. And I did because this nation most needs someone that believes in people above party, above self, above any special interest, no matter the cost to one. So as I told my staff and we got in, I said, look, we're going to aim to be on the fall debates at some time. I said, I can't complain about the rules. I landed on this beach from the landing craft. And you don't complain about the rules that happen to be there when you land and go back to the landing craft. You deal with them, but I would make a recommendation for years from now that if you are going to measure at properly support for a candidate, then look at the two criteria that have been established. One of them is polling. That makes sense. How much do they show their support for you? But the other one was money. And whenever you make money a criteria, even in taxes, when you change and somebody will always find a loophole. And so you can have somebody come along and understandably, and I'm not complaining at all, but somebody will put millions of dollars in this happen and then be able to say about 130,000 supporters after they pound away with me dollars. Does that show support",
