    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "And if I could take it one more step, you know, I ran against my party's desires. I represent nearly first off to one Republican district, nearly to the one. And I guess the second Democrats since the Civil War. But despite a F from the NRA, or my rating, despite 100% voting record from the pro-choice, May Realtors' Choice, I got reelected by 20 points and I didn't spend a penny on a campaign ad. We learned to disagree well and we could do I could stand by my principles but do principle compromise. But, you know, I also ran against my party's desires when Senator Arlen Specter, the senator who had years ago earlier humiliated, tried to humiliate Anita Hill, who had brought sexual harassment claims against now Supreme Court Justice Clarence Thomas. And my party years decades later was going to embrace this man. I disagree if it was today with the Me Too generation, my party would have done it. But accountability means doing what's right when it matters. So I ran against my party's desires, beat the senator after he'd become a Democrat, after being a Republican so long. They came at a cost, and I bring both of those two issues up, because I am most running, Jared, that these wonderful policies you've given me the opportunity to talk about. or great, but in order to advance from, we are going to need someone in that White House that can beat Mr. Trump, that can unite this nation because people feel that he is accountable to them, and they will trust him even when they disagree well, and someone who can convene the world because of a breadth and depth of experience on that candidate. And that's the reason I am running most, because if we don't unite this country, we will not be able to meet the defining challenges of our time. And that is why when my daughter recovered for brain cancer, I decided to get in. And why I say I'm not late, I think I'm timely, because that's what Americans most yearn for.",
