    "turn_text": "Yes. What I would leave with is a story about the youth of America, which is where you started, Jared. As I said, come aboard that aircraft carrier with a 5,000 sailors. And I told you I learned from them. And let me give you an example. When a carrier, middle of the night, you know, is launching planes, a pilot gets in and they strap themselves in the plane and then close the canopy and then they hook up the plane to a catapult. It's a little sled. And when they push a button, that sled pushes the plane with its engines running into the night. And there's no rides like that in any amusement park. I can tell you that. But sometimes they say, stop. Just as your engines and you're about to push the buck and you're ready to go. And the plane's bucking ready to go. But they need a different plane over Afghanistan because it's been an ambush. And they need different types of fighters over there, not what was going to go up. And so a young man or woman could be from California, could be from Iowa, could be from a red state of blue state, could be Muslim, could be Hispanic, could be white. We just don't care. We get them all and we love them all and we mow them together. And one of them comes out on that deck in the middle of the night, reaches under the plane with a pilot can't see and unhooks the plane from the catapults. And because the pilot can't feel, but wants to really feel it's definitely been unhooked. Because once you turn off your plane, you're still strapped to that catapult and someone makes a mistake and pushes the button. You're going to go off into the night for a wonderful, but it's your last ride. So that youth doesn't step to the side of the plane and signal the pilot. He or she has done the job. Jared, he walks or she walks in front of that plane and looks up at the pilot and raises the left hand with a little signal. And then that youth of America doesn't move until that pilot has shut off his or her engines, opened up the canopy of the plane and gotten safely on that. And that youth has said everything, this nation most yearns for and most wants. Go ahead, that young man or woman has said, pilot, you can trust me, not for my word, but for my being, because if I made a mistake and suddenly after you turn off your engines, Because of my mistake, you suddenly start going forward to your death. You're going right through me and I'm going overboard with you to my own. Jared, I have met hardly anyone who believes that",
